==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[pro tempore]] - US Constitution, Amendment XXV (1967), Section 3.

===Etymology===
From the {{L.}} phrase; ''[[pro#Latin|pro]] [[tempus#Latin|tempore]]''. The proposition ''[[pro#Latin|pro]]'' means "[[for]]" and ''[[tempore#Latin|tempore]]'' is the {{abl}} of ''[[tempus#Latin|tempus]]'' meaning "[[time]]".
===Adverb===
'''pro tem'''
# [[temporarily]]; for the time being

===Adjective===
'''pro tem'''
# [[temporary]]